  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models substantially outperform image-only (0.485-0.520 vs 0.208), and scvi_n200 beats pca_n2000 (0.520 vs 0.485), establishing scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder so far. The critical unresolved question is whether multiprofile representation (with aggregation) adds value over singleprofile. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares against config_004 (same encoder, singleprofile) by changing only the profile setting and adding the simplest aggregation (avgpool). It isolates the multiprofile effect without confounding with a more complex aggregation (transformer) or a new encoder (scgpt). If multiprofile+avgpool improves over 0.520, it validates the multiprofile axis and justifies testing transformer aggregation next; if it does not, a large portion of the search space (all multiprofile configs) can be deprioritized, saving budget for the more promising multimodal or encoder-comparison directions. This is the highest-information single step under the limited budget."
}

